# 4. ADMIN USER COMMUNICATION — PING, NOTIFICATIONS & LIVE UPDATES

Create a communication system that allows Admin to send messages or notifications to users.

The purpose is to allow important announcements, gentle reminders, updates, and personalized communication.

This should not become an intrusive system.

## 4.1 Admin ping

Add an Admin action called "Ping User" or "Send Notification".

Admin should be able to:

- Select a user
- Write a short message
- Choose notification type
- Preview the message
- Send or schedule it, if supported

Notification categories may include:

- General message
- Important announcement
- Gentle reminder
- App update
- Affirmation
- Personal encouragement

Keep messages respectful, calm and non-judgmental.

Avoid language that pressures users for not checking in, not writing journal entries, or being inactive.

## 4.2 Notification experience for users

Create an attractive notification system for the main Lunara app.

Include:

- Notification icon
- Unread indicator
- Notification center
- Notification list
- Notification timestamps
- Read/unread status
- Mark as read
- Mark all as read
- Dismiss/delete where appropriate
- Notification preferences

Notifications should use a clean and readable layout.

Use appropriate iconography and color identities for different notification categories.

## 4.3 Live updates

Design the system to support real-time or near-real-time updates in the future.

Examples:

- Admin sends a message → user sees the notification.
- Admin updates an affirmation → content can refresh.
- Admin publishes a new Gita learning → the content appears in the appropriate section.
- Admin updates application content → the relevant pages receive the update.

Architecture should be prepared for future realtime functionality through Supabase Realtime, notifications or another appropriate backend service.

However, the database and backend are currently deferred.

Therefore:

- Implement the frontend communication interface.
- Create a clearly isolated notification state/service layer.
- Use mock events only where necessary.
- Do not pretend notifications are truly live across different accounts or devices.
- Do not implement a fake websocket or realtime system that falsely claims to be operational.
- Clearly distinguish prototype behavior from real backend functionality.

## 4.4 User notification settings

Allow users to control the types of messages they receive.

Include appropriate preferences such as:

- Affirmations
- Daily wisdom
- Gentle reminders
- Admin messages
- Announcements

Allow notification preferences to be toggled.

Do not assume all notifications should be enabled.

