## Content accuracy requirements

The Bhagavad Gita is a real scripture. Content accuracy matters.

- Do not fabricate verses.
- Do not invent chapter/verse references.
- Do not generate incorrect Sanskrit text.
- Do not create mismatched transliterations.
- Do not falsely attribute modern reflections to Krishna or the scripture.
- Distinguish original scripture, translation, interpretation and modern takeaway.
- Use verified source material for scripture and translations.
- When the source is uncertain, do not publish the entry as verified.
- Use original explanations for Lunara's learnings.
- Maintain the source/reference information for each entry.

For the frontend prototype, use a small carefully verified collection instead of generating dozens of questionable entries.

Admin must be able to update the content later without requiring a redesign of the Wisdom page.

